---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from "../lib/site";
import { breadcrumbSchema, organizationSchema } from "../lib/schema";

/** Updated whenever the policy text changes. */
const lastUpdated = "October 23, 2026";

const jsonLd = [
    organizationSchema(),
    breadcrumbSchema([
        { name: "Home", path: "/" },
        { name: "Privacy Policy", path: "/privacy-policy/" },
    ]),
];
---

<Layout
    title="Privacy Policy — CleanBoard"
    description="How CleanBoard handles your data: typing stays on your device, there are no ads or tracking, and the optional internet features are off until you turn them on."
    path="/privacy-policy/"
    jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
    <div class="container container--reading">
        <article class="prose policy">
            <header class="policy__head">
                <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
                <p class="policy__meta">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
            </header>

            <p>
                CleanBoard is built by heymeowcat. This policy explains what
                happens to your data. The short version: the keyboard is
                offline-first, there are no ads and no tracking, and the few
                features that can use the internet are off until you choose to
                turn them on.
            </p>

            <h2 id="stays-on-device">1. What stays on your device</h2>
            <p>
                Typing, Singlish transliteration, spelling correction, word
                prediction, the bundled English and Sinhala dictionaries, your
                personal dictionary, learned words and clipboard history are
                processed and stored locally on your device. CleanBoard does not
                send your keystrokes, typed text or clipboard to us.
            </p>
            <p>
                Settings and the personal dictionary live in the app&rsquo;s
                private storage. Clipboard history and the learned-word history
                are deliberately excluded from Android cloud backup and device
                transfer. Other app data, such as settings and the personal
                dictionary, may be included if you have Android&rsquo;s backup
                service enabled; that backup is controlled by your device and
                your Android backup settings, not by CleanBoard.
            </p>

            <h2 id="optional-internet">2. Optional features that use the internet</h2>
            <p>
                CleanBoard requests the Android <code>INTERNET</code> permission
                because a few optional features can use a network connection.
                Each of them is off by default and only works after you enable
                it:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <strong>GIF and sticker search</strong> — when you open the
                    GIF or sticker tab, the app contacts Klipy&rsquo;s API
                    (<code>api.klipy.com</code>) to load trending results or the
                    search term you type. Klipy receives that request and
                    standard network information such as your IP address, and
                    handles it under its own
                    <a href="https://klipy.com/support/privacy-policy" rel="noopener" target="_blank">privacy policy</a>.
                    CleanBoard has no Klipy account and does not send your name,
                    email address or keyboard history.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Voice input</strong> — the microphone button uses
                    Android&rsquo;s speech recognition service. When you use it,
                    audio is passed to the speech recognition provider selected
                    by your device, which may process it on-device or on its own
                    servers depending on the provider and your device settings.
                    CleanBoard does not store the audio and does not receive the
                    provider&rsquo;s recordings.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Optional model and dictionary downloads</strong> —
                    if you choose to download an updated prediction model or the
                    optional translation dictionary, the app fetches the file
                    from GitHub. GitHub receives a standard file request,
                    including your IP address.
                </li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                If you never enable these features, the keyboard does not use
                the network. You can turn each one off again at any time from
                the Privacy section of the app&rsquo;s home screen.
            </p>

            <h2 id="permissions">3. Permissions</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <strong>Internet</strong> — used only by the optional
                    features described above.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Microphone</strong> — requested only when you turn on
                    voice input and tap the microphone button. You can deny or
                    revoke it in Android settings; the rest of the keyboard keeps
                    working.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Vibration</strong> — used for haptic feedback if you
                    enable it. Vibration is a normal Android capability rather
                    than a runtime permission on current versions.
                </li>
            </ul>

            <h2 id="no-tracking">4. No advertising, analytics or accounts</h2>
            <p>
                CleanBoard has no advertising SDK, no analytics SDK, no
                crash-reporting SDK, no fingerprinting and no account system.
                We do not sell data, build advertising profiles or track you
                across apps. There is no CleanBoard server that receives your
                typing.
            </p>

            <h2 id="website">5. This website</h2>
            <p>
                The website at <code>heymeowcat.is-a.dev/cleanboard-site</code>
                is a static site. It sets no cookies, runs no analytics and
                embeds no third-party scripts. The English-to-Sinhala converter
                runs entirely inside your browser using JavaScript served from
                this domain; the text you type is never transmitted anywhere.
            </p>
            <p>
                Links to Google Play, GitHub and Klipy take you to those
                services when you click them. Those services have their own
                privacy policies.
            </p>

            <h2 id="third-party">6. Third-party services</h2>
            <p>
                If you download CleanBoard from Google Play, Google Play handles
                the transaction and collects the data described in its own
                privacy policy. If you contact us by email, your message travels
                through your own mail provider. The optional GIF/sticker search,
                voice input and file downloads involve the third parties named
                in section 2.
            </p>

            <h2 id="children">7. Children</h2>
            <p>
                CleanBoard is intended for general audiences. We do not knowingly
                collect personal information from children, because we do not
                collect personal information from anyone.
            </p>

            <h2 id="changes">8. Changes to this policy</h2>
            <p>
                If this policy changes, the update will be published on this
                page with a new &ldquo;last updated&rdquo; date. Material changes
                will also be mentioned in the app&rsquo;s release notes.
            </p>

            <h2 id="contact">9. Contact</h2>
            <p>
                Questions about this policy can be sent to
                <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
            </p>
        </article>
    </div>
</Layout>

<style>
    .policy {
        padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem) 1rem;
    }

    .policy__head {
        margin-bottom: 2rem;
        padding-bottom: 1.5rem;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    }

    .policy h1 {
        font-size: clamp(1.875rem, 5vw, 2.5rem);
    }

    .policy__meta {
        margin-top: 0.5rem;
        font-size: 0.875rem;
    }
</style>
